label chapter_1_3:

    scene bg RECOG HALL GARDEN
    with dissolve

    nvl clear

    show sofia b casual clfrown:
        xoffset -250
        zoom 1.25
        alpha 0.90
    with Dissolve(1)

    n "I tried so hard to ignore her. She's unbearable to talk to, she says the most unbearable things, and she makes nods to things that frankly I don't even care to think of.{w}"
    show sofia b casual clfrown:
        xoffset -400
        yoffset -100
        zoom 1.5
        alpha 0.70
    with Dissolve(1)
    extend " Regrettably, I know what she's talking about half the time. Our parents made us watch TV all the time, and she had the expensive kind. Cable.{w}"
    show sofia a casual silook:
        xoffset -650
        yoffset -200
        zoom 2
        alpha 0.50
    with Dissolve(1)
    extend " I have cable at my home, too, but I don't care to click through any of the channels. I already have my home computer to attend to. She'd always put the anime channel on cable. We'd do the stupid dances together and sing the songs in broken pretend-foreign-language. I still have notebooks with those Pretty Beat stickers she gave me on the front. When I tried to peel them off the covers were only damaged, so I kept them in a drawer, covered in ash and perhaps growing mold. One of the notebooks had a lopsided drawing of hers in it. I only broke them open again to use as scratch paper for my math homework."

    nvl clear
    show sofia a casual neutral1 at loc(300):
        alpha 1
        yoffset 0
        zoom 1
    show sharlene casual side_look at loc(450)
    with Dissolve(3)
    n "Sharlene plays with her hands in the most anxious way. It's like watching a small animal. Whenever she's not rubbing the skin on her fingers against her palm, she's scratching at every piece of loose skin she can find. She picks and I notice this every time, but she has the hands of a brute. Crackled, peeled skin at the edges of all of her nails. She always picks at them even when they're already bleeding. She was picking at them again. The red seeped out and her hands floated up to bite on the already bleeding hangnail. I swear I caught myself involuntarily dry hacking."

    show sofia a casual neutral1 at loc(500)
    with moveinright
    show sharlene casual side_look with hpunch
    n "I raised my palm to slap her hand away from her face. She didn't even react. At some point, she stopped reacting strongly. She always cried before when I would hurt her in any way, even when it was just dumb things like accidentally ribbing her or accidentally catching my nails in her hair. She'd cry and scream so loud her parents thought I was killing her."

    n "Sometimes, I don't think they’re wrong. I've tried to kill her so many times in my mind, already."

    return